  "difficulty": 2,
  "prompt": "A pendulum returns to its starting position whenever $\\cos\\theta = 1$. What is the general solution of $\\cos\\theta = 1$?",
  "answerType": "multiple-choice",
  "choices": [
    {
      "id": "A",
      "label": "$\\theta = 360^\\circ k$ for every integer $k$",
      "correct": true
    },
    {
      "id": "B",
      "label": "$\\theta = 180^\\circ k$ for every integer $k$",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "C",
      "label": "$\\theta = 0^\\circ$ and $\\theta = 360^\\circ$ only",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "D",
      "label": "$\\theta = 90^\\circ + 360^\\circ k$ for every integer $k$",
      "correct": false
    }
  ],
  "primaryAnswer": "A",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "exact",
  "hint": "Cosine reaches its maximum of $1$ only at the very right of the unit circle.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "Cosine reaches its maximum of $1$ only at the very right of the unit circle."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "That happens once per full turn, so the solutions are spaced $360^\\circ$ apart."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "$\\theta = 0^\\circ, \\pm 360^\\circ, \\pm 720^\\circ, \\ldots$, which is $\\theta = 360^\\circ k$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "$\\cos\\theta = 1$ only at the point $(1, 0)$ on the unit circle, which is angle $0^\\circ$.",
    "Every full revolution returns to that same point, and a full revolution is $360^\\circ$.",
    "So the general solution is $\\theta = 360^\\circ k$ for any integer $k$ — the pendulum comes home once per complete swing cycle."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Why $180^\\circ k$ is wrong",
      "steps": [
        "Choice B would include $\\theta = 180^\\circ$, but $\\cos 180^\\circ = -1$, not $1$.",
        "That is the pendulum at the far end of its swing, the opposite of where it started.",
        "Maximum values repeat once per period, so the spacing is a full $360^\\circ$."
      ]
    }
  ],
